Pros:
+ nice soundtrack;
+ voice acting is tolerable;
+ not too short;
+ nice art;
+ I liked the background history books with a little game of placing objects where they belong, the art is lovely.
Cons:
- a lot of pointless 'tasks', made to prolong the game process, such as: one click to insert a key, one click to turn the key, one click to open the door/chest, etc;
- more point&click tasks and mini-games that I can tolerate in a HOG;
- illogical application of objects (like, you know, setting up a BOMB inside a house to put away a folding screen? WTF? or being able to interact with an object only with a specific knife, even if you already have another knife in your inventory);
- sometimes more than one object fitting a description in a hidden objest scene, but only one of them is a correct answer.
6/10.
